  "answers": [
    "Your reliable average for October 1\u20133 is **6,000 steps per day**, but it rests on a single day, October 3.\n\n- **Oct 1:** There are no step records, so the day is missing. It isn't counted as zero.\n- **Oct 2:** The record shows 0 steps. Fitbit treats a 0-step day like that as no-wear, so this is probably the day the watch was off.\n- **Oct 3:** 6,000 steps.\n\nThe summary tool's headline mean was 3,000 steps per day, which averages 6,000 and 0 over 2 days. That number counts the 0-step day even though the same summary flags it as no-wear, so I wouldn't trust it. It would understate your activity.\n\nTwo of the three days have no usable data, so you can't tell whether 6,000 is typical for you. Oct 1 has no records at all, so the watch may have been off then, not on Oct 2. It may also just not have synced. I can run a sync to check whether Oct 1 fills in if you'd like."
